e explicitly does not solve the R3 Kakeya maximal-function conjecture with K=3; higher-dimensional dimension problems are also separate.", "status": "selected preprint statements read; full proof not independently verified", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No full proof reconstruction or formal verification performed by this atlas; selected theorem scope was compared with foundational definitions.", "nextQuestions": ["Inspect subsequent revisions and independent assessments after this dated corpus.", "Reconstruct the full theorem assumptions before transferring the result to a different setting."], "title": "Volume estimates for unions of convex sets, and the Kakeya set conjecture in three dimensions", "kind": "paper", "domain": "mathematics"}</data></node><node id="math-paper-langlands"><data key="title">Proof of the geometric Langlands conjecture I: construction of the functor</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">mathematics</data><data key="status">selected preprint statements read; full proof not independently verified</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "math-paper-langlands", "sourceId": "math-langlands", "topicIds": ["math-geometric-langlands"], "question": "How can automorphic and spectral categories be connected in characteristic zero?", "method": "Categorical construction and comparison of deRham/Betti and tempered/restricted formulations.", "result": "PartI constructs one direction of the functor and proves specified equivalences.", "whatIsNew": "The inspected contribution is a functor construction and framework comparison, not an atlas proof of every Langlands conjecture.", "limitations": "PartI is not by itself the complete multi-paper proof, arithmetic Langlands or every coefficient/characteristic setting. The inspected characteristic-zero global/unramified setup fixes a smooth complete curve X and connected reductive G; PartI is one of five papers.", "status": "selected preprint statements read; full proof not independently verifie